            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and analgesic activity of 2-phenoxybenzoic acid and N-phenylanthranilic acid hydrazides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1180-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of 2-phenoxybenzoic acid and N-phenylanthranilic acid hydrazides were synthesized and evaluated for their analgesic activities. Several compounds were significantly more potent than mefenamic acid and diclofenac sodium in abdominal constriction and formalin tests.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
